## 0. HOW TO WORK (read first)

1. Inspect the existing Mirai frontend: framework, router, styling system (Tailwind/CSS modules/etc.), component library, data layer, API clients, player implementation, auth/profile logic.
2. Map each screen below to its existing route/component (Home, Browse, Anime Detail, Watch, Profile Edit, Continue Watching, Settings, plus shared Navbar and Footer).
3. Do a **performance baseline measurement first** (Section 10), then redesign, then re-measure.
4. Build shared primitives first (tokens, glass surface, buttons, chips, poster card, section header, toggle, input), then screens.
5. Never replace real data with the sample data seen in the screenshots (titles, usernames, emails, temporary passwords, dates are examples only).
6. Anything not covered by references: reuse the closest design language from these screens with restrained creativity.

